      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The period leading up to the 1952 **pre- and immediate aftermath of the 1940s** saw intense anti-colonial sentiment and a deep sense of political and economic oppression under the British in the former \"White Highlands,\" driving the need for a fight for self-determination. The **1952 start of the Uprising** was a powerful, desperate response to systematic discriminatory policies, forced labor, and the denial of political rights to the local population in the face of staunch and often brutal enforcement by the colonial state.\n\nThe **war period (1952-1960s in certain strong pro-s\n\n The **end of the Uprising and the political shift in the 1950s and 19\n\n This period ultimately forced the political elite to negotiate for a more decisive end to the discriminatory political and social power of the colonial regime, leading to the push for greater self-rule for the people.",
